  "explanation": "The quoted inference is false: a nonincreasing positive integer sequence can reach 0, and indeed K strictly drops by 1 at every coprime move, so monotonicity alone gives nothing. The needed fact is that each move outputs at least one nonunit. The write-up supplies this only in the coprime case (\"the new entries are 1 and mn\", i.e. mn>1) and, as an example, for equal entries; for a general move with g>1 it never states that gcd(m,n)=g>1 is a nonunit output. Hence \"exactly one nonunit remains\" rests on the false lemma flagged in the rubric. One added sentence covering the g>1 case repairs it."
